w('<h2>8. Shear anchors A2: shear on the concrete side</h2>');
w(['<p>Two concrete failures exist in shear, and only one of them is a cone. <b>Pryout</b> (17.7.3) is the tension cone again: the stubby anchor levers about the concrete it bears on at the face, its end nut lifts, and it pulls a cone out behind it, so its strength is k<sub>cp</sub> N<sub>cb</sub>. ' ...
   '<b>Shear breakout</b> (17.7.2) is a different body: a half cone pushed out towards the free edge the shear points at. It depends on the distance to that edge, c<sub>a1</sub>, and hardly on h<sub>ef</sub> (only through l<sub>e</sub>). ' ...
   'The first version of the calculation had steel and pryout, and dismissed breakout because V points down where the column goes on. It missed two things: the torsion couple H pushes the shear anchors across the beam, towards a free side face, and ACI also checks a shear that runs <i>parallel</i> to an edge (17.7.2.1(c)). Both are below.</p>']);
