  Vs*kN, R.typ(1).Tor*1e-6, R.typ(1).Tor*1e-6, (R.typ(1).zT - S.zS)/1e3, Hs*kN);
w('<li>Up: the uplift combination 0.9D &minus; E<sub>v</sub> still leaves q = %.2f kN/m&sup2; down, so V never points to the top of the pedestal. Down: the column goes on below the cold joint (not a free edge), so no breakout downward.</li>', R.q(3));
w('<li>Pryout body (figure I): 1.5 h<sub>ef</sub> = %g from the axes at the face. Across: %g + 2 &times; min(c<sub>a</sub> = %g, %g) = %.0f; up and down: min(%.0f, %g) + %g = %.0f. A<sub>Nc</sub> = %.0f &times; %.0f = %.0f mm&sup2;, A<sub>Nco</sub> = 9 h<sub>ef</sub>&sup2; = %.0f mm&sup2;.</li>', ...
  1.5*S.hef, 2*an.vS, P.col.b/2 - an.vS, 1.5*S.hef, 2*min(P.col.b/2 - an.vS, 1.5*S.hef) + 2*an.vS, S.ctop, 1.5*S.hef, 1.5*S.hef, min(S.ctop, 1.5*S.hef) + 1.5*S.hef, ...
  2*min(P.col.b/2 - an.vS, 1.5*S.hef) + 2*an.vS, min(S.ctop, 1.5*S.hef) + 1.5*S.hef, S.ANc, S.ANco);
w('<li>N<sub>b</sub> = k<sub>c</sub> &lambda; &radic;f''<sub>c</sub> h<sub>ef</sub><sup>1.5</sup> = 10 &times; %.2f &times; %g<sup>1.5</sup> = %.1f kN (cast-in, k<sub>c</sub> = 10; cracked, &psi;<sub>c,N</sub> = 1); &psi;<sub>ed,N</sub> = %.2f (c<sub>a,min</sub> = %g &ge; 1.5 h<sub>ef</sub>); &psi;<sub>ec,N</sub> = 1.</li>', sq, S.hef, S.Nb*kN, S.pedN, P.col.b/2 - an.vS);
w('<li>N<sub>cbg</sub> = (%.0f/%.0f) &times; %.2f &times; %.1f = %.1f kN; &phi;V<sub>cpg</sub> = 0.70 &times; k<sub>cp</sub> N<sub>cbg</sub> = 0.70 &times; 2 &times; %.1f = <b>%.1f kN</b> (k<sub>cp</sub> = 2 for h<sub>ef</sub> &ge; 65).</li>', S.ANc, S.ANco, S.pedN, S.Nb*kN, S.Ncbg*kN, S.Ncbg*kN, S.phiVcp*kN);
w('<li class="ok">V on the group &radic;(V&sup2; + H&sup2;) = %.1f kN; D/C %.2f</li>', S.Vg(1)*kN, S.Vg(1)/S.phiVcp);
w('<li>The lower edge of the body reaches the cold joint at %g (1 mm past it). A cold joint is not an edge: the column below is the same member, tied through by the column bars. The end-plate compression of the moment (C = T, near the bottom flange) presses on this body; ACI does not count it.</li>', P.col.cj);
