   'ACI has no rule for a shear inclined to the edge; EN 1992-4 (7.2.2.5, &psi;<sub>&alpha;,V</sub>) combines them as V<sub>res</sub>/V<sub>cb,&alpha;</sub> = &radic;[(V<sub>&perp;</sub>/V<sub>cb</sub>)&sup2; + (V<sub>&#8741;</sub>/2V<sub>cb</sub>)&sup2;], which is what the calc uses.</li>'], ...
   Hs/2*kN, S.phiVb(1)*kN, Hs/2/S.phiVb(1), Vs/2*kN, S.phiVp(1)*kN, Vs/2/S.phiVp(1), Hs*kN, S.phiVb(2)*kN, Hs/S.phiVb(2), Vs*kN, S.phiVp(2)*kN, Vs/S.phiVp(2));
w('<li class="ok">Case 1: &radic;(%.2f&sup2; + %.2f&sup2;) = %.2f. Case 2: &radic;(%.2f&sup2; + %.2f&sup2;) = %.2f, governs.</li>', Hs/2/S.phiVb(1), Vs/2/S.phiVp(1), sqrt(S.ell1(1)), Hs/S.phiVb(2), Vs/S.phiVp(2), sqrt(S.ell2(1)));
w('<li>Figure K shows the bodies on the face of the cantilever: the pryout area A<sub>Nc</sub> (blue), and where each breakout half cone comes out on this face (red, orange). The orange one is cut by the top of the pedestal, hence &psi;<sub>ed,V</sub> &lt; 1 in case 2.</li>');
