% ---- 8b. top anchors in shear
St = R.sht;  j4 = 4;  Y4 = R.typ(j4);
w('<h2>8b. Top anchors A1 in shear</h2>');
w(['<p><b>Which way the shear goes decides where the cone is.</b> A shear breakout opens towards the free face the shear points at. V points down: below the top anchors there are %.0f mm of concrete to the shear anchors and the whole column after them, so there is no cone downward. ' ...
   'The %g mm of concrete above them (%g at CY) is on the side <i>away</i> from V. That is where a pryout crater would open, and pryout is checked with the cone cut by the top. ' ...
   'The shear that does point at a free face is the torsion couple H, across the beam towards a side face, and the top of the pedestal cuts that half cone (figure L).</p>'], Y.zT - S.zS, P.col.top - Y.zT, P.col.top - R.typ(4).zT);
w(['<p><b>What the top anchors carry.</b> The calculation gives V to the shear anchors (they are designed for all of it). The top anchors always carry H: it is half of the torsion couple, and it cannot move to the shear anchors. ' ...
   'If the four holes of the end plate bore at once, each top anchor would also take V/4. That is checked too, as information.</p>']);
w('<div class="row"><div><img src="figures/ta_stop.png" alt="top anchors shear"></div><div class="calc"><ol>');
w(['<li>Breakout to a side face, as for the shear anchors (17.7.2, cases 1 and 2), now with the top of the pedestal at c<sub>a2</sub> = %g (CY): l<sub>e</sub> = min(h<sub>ef</sub>, 8 d<sub>a</sub>) = %g. ' ...
   'Case 1 (c<sub>a1</sub> = %g): A<sub>Vc</sub> = (%g + %.0f) &times; %.0f = %.0f mm&sup2; of A<sub>Vco</sub> = %.0f, &psi;<sub>ed,V</sub> = %.2f: &phi;V<sub>cb</sub> = <b>%.1f kN</b> across, %.1f kN parallel. ' ...
   'Case 2 (c<sub>a1</sub> = %g): A<sub>Vc</sub>/A<sub>Vco</sub> = %.2f, &psi;<sub>ed,V</sub> = %.2f: &phi;V<sub>cb</sub> = <b>%.1f kN</b> across, %.1f kN parallel.</li>'], ...
   St.ctop(j4), St.le, St.ca1(1), St.ctop(j4), 1.5*St.ca1(1), 1.5*St.ca1(1), St.Avc(1,j4), St.Avco(1,j4), St.pedV(1,j4), St.phiVb(1,j4)*kN, St.phiVp(1,j4)*kN, ...
   St.ca1(2), St.Avc(2,j4)/St.Avco(2,j4), St.pedV(2,j4), St.phiVb(2,j4)*kN, St.phiVp(2,j4)*kN);
w('<li>Pryout of the pair (17.7.3): &phi;V<sub>cpg</sub> = 0.70 &times; 2 N<sub>cbg</sub> with the unreinforced cone of section 6 (h''<sub>ef</sub> = %.0f, cut by the top and both sides): %.1f kN (CY), %.1f kN (E).</li>', R.brk(j4).hefp, St.phiVcp(j4)*kN, St.phiVcp(1)*kN);
w('<li>H on the pair at CY: %.1f kN. Shear ratios with H alone: case 1 %.2f, case 2 <b>%.2f</b>, pryout %.2f, steel %.2f.</li>', Y4.Hc*kN, St.b1(1,j4), St.b2(1,j4), St.cp(1,j4), St.sa(1,j4));
